<item>
<title>Nigeria: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/nigeria/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-nigeria-2026-10-24T07:29:10.368Z</guid>
<pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:29:10 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen killed an NSCDC officer and abducted a businessman in Plateau despite a curfew, and gunmen attacked an Ebonyi assembly candidate convoy, killing one and injuring three. In Benue, suspected herders killed three civilians and Senate leaders are demanding a security overhaul and troop deployment after 113 people were killed, while electricity workers withdrew services in Makurdi following an alleged attack. Bandits continue to hold a widow, her son and a newborn captive three weeks after a kidnapping in Kaduna, and a NDC supporter was killed in Enugu. Floods killed 245 people and displaced over 200,000, according to NEMA, and the conflict produced 1,486 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/23/france-police-demonstrations-civil-unrest&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-french-police-deploy-in-big-numbers-and-paris-shuts-major-museums-ahead-of-new-protests&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiAFBVV95cUxPdDZORDh0Y0V5N1dWRnl0NVlFSGktX2JvZWt2S0VKUWk0MkV1Y0dWUXp4M016QkJLWmRFS0Q4N3hpcWpNRlpQTDFJMDZhaG85RENJQlZTd1piQU40ZkhJQ1dLR2pZdEloVnluY1k2QnhERzFyZ1VPc0NfVVNTektuQnlYdTdjeE9f?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxOMFk0enRkelZfRmk3UmpqYlg5Z1RSaHpWbVVjSFBFVFg1enh1alBoRHFDTlI5RG5vVFNjZHZjQUJyZFEyeXBYdjJGTDRZTHg3X3BncExiSUFJT1ZNYWY3UUhPX2t5WXVVRFlwZHRaaEZKbUpSUnlZSk5WTkNxZGt0eTV6Q3Z4ZWFqdS1jZWF0ZEpia0ctLTRuY0UyTlZzSkN4UHByVl93bVdGaUxTd1lQOU1vZTcyTUpKa1E?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqgFBVV95cUxPVXItNmFOcy1xTnAzMnJzNXpXQ193ZWZSWGp4U0tPVGd4Slc5aS02Zk5EYUtTbmJRemNqczhVdEdzTzY